1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,872
Monday, ten in the morning.

2
00:00:01,922 --> 00:00:07,128
Aziz sits in a café, on the café Wi-Fi, and logs in to the mobile bank.

3
00:00:07,178 --> 00:00:10,536
He types his password, then the code from the SMS.

4
00:00:10,586 --> 00:00:15,168
It is the right code, and still the app says: We cannot complete this now.

5
00:00:15,218 --> 00:00:19,592
Why would a platform refuse a correct code?

6
00:00:19,642 --> 00:00:25,736
The counters of Lesson 9 guard the code itself: its life, its tries, its requests.

7
00:00:25,786 --> 00:00:29,264
They cannot see where the code arrived, but TAF can.

8
00:00:29,314 --> 00:00:33,032
And TAF works only in the master app, the mobile bank.

9
00:00:33,082 --> 00:00:35,288
First, what TAF is.

10
00:00:35,338 --> 00:00:37,856
It is a state service of the mobile operators.

11
00:00:37,906 --> 00:00:43,808
Its agent already runs in the bank's network, and heeyID talks to it only through its TAF adapter.

12
00:00:43,858 --> 00:00:49,160
In the master app, TAF sends every code for a registration and a login.

13
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:54,224
Its part inside the app checks that the SMS arrived on this phone, with this SIM card.

14
00:00:54,274 --> 00:00:56,696
Then TAF gives a verdict.

15
00:00:56,746 --> 00:01:00,176
The most important word in this lesson is recommendation.

16
00:01:00,226 --> 00:01:02,048
The verdict is advice.

17
00:01:02,098 --> 00:01:05,696
The platform makes the decision, with the policy of the bank.

18
00:01:05,746 --> 00:01:07,568
The app has a job too.

19
00:01:07,618 --> 00:01:10,400
It starts the TAF part after an install.

20
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:13,952
It sends the identifier of that part with each code request.

21
00:01:14,002 --> 00:01:17,768
It gives each typed code to the TAF part first.

22
00:01:17,818 --> 00:01:21,176
And it tells the TAF part at each logout.

23
00:01:21,226 --> 00:01:25,040
If the app skips a step, the verdict simply comes back negative.

24
00:01:25,090 --> 00:01:29,624
After a correct code, the platform asks TAF for two verdicts.

25
00:01:29,674 --> 00:01:43,592
The basic verdict is seven plain answers: the account is active, the code is usable, the SMS was sent, the status is valid, the code was verified, the device and the SIM card match, and the phone is not a clone.

26
00:01:43,642 --> 00:01:48,752
The risk verdict is a colour: Green, Yellow or Red, with a main reason.

27
00:01:48,802 --> 00:01:55,664
The risk verdict can take a moment, so the platform asks again at a set interval, until the configured waiting time ends.

28
00:01:55,714 --> 00:01:59,096
If it is still not ready, the basic verdict decides.

29
00:01:59,146 --> 00:02:01,520
All seven answers true means Green.

30
00:02:01,570 --> 00:02:03,392
One false answer means Red.

31
00:02:03,442 --> 00:02:09,176
The platform records the result, where it came from, and whether the device and the SIM card matched.

32
00:02:09,226 --> 00:02:11,792
Lesson 16 needs that SIM match.

33
00:02:11,842 --> 00:02:13,664
Back to the café.

34
00:02:13,714 --> 00:02:16,112
The risk verdict did not arrive in time.

35
00:02:16,162 --> 00:02:22,184
On the café Wi-Fi, the device and the SIM card did not match, so the basic verdict said Red.

36
00:02:22,234 --> 00:02:24,056
Red means refuse.

37
00:02:24,106 --> 00:02:25,928
The login attempt ends.

38
00:02:25,978 --> 00:02:29,576
But a refusal blocks nothing, and it changes no counter.

39
00:02:29,626 --> 00:02:35,048
The app shows one piece of advice: use the mobile network of your operator, not Wi-Fi.

40
00:02:35,098 --> 00:02:37,976
Aziz switches off the Wi-Fi and tries again.

41
00:02:38,026 --> 00:02:41,768
This time the risk verdict arrives in time, and it is Green.

42
00:02:41,818 --> 00:02:44,936
The login continues, with the SIM match on record.

43
00:02:44,986 --> 00:02:47,144
Yellow is the careful colour.

44
00:02:47,194 --> 00:02:53,504
It also means refuse, with the reason text of TAF, in the language of the journey.

45
00:02:53,554 --> 00:02:58,088
The texts come from the configuration of the bank, and again, nothing is blocked.

46
00:02:58,138 --> 00:03:02,144
Aziz is at level one, so his login asks for nothing more.

47
00:03:02,194 --> 00:03:07,280
At level two, a login after Green also asks for the face biometric of the phone.

48
00:03:07,330 --> 00:03:10,208
This is not MyID, and it gives no level.

49
00:03:10,258 --> 00:03:15,296
If the face check of the phone fails, the login stops, and the customer can try again.

50
00:03:15,346 --> 00:03:21,224
If the phone has no face biometric at all, the login continues, and nothing goes to TAF.

51
00:03:21,274 --> 00:03:28,928
When the check succeeds, the platform sends a face confirmation to TAF, with the personal identification number and the phone number.

52
00:03:28,978 --> 00:03:34,784
The platform sends it, never the app, so the personal identification number never reaches the phone.

53
00:03:34,834 --> 00:03:41,576
If TAF does not answer, the login still continues, and the confirmation waits for the next login.

54
00:03:41,626 --> 00:03:46,784
The same confirmation also comes before the phone ownership check of Lesson 15.

55
00:03:46,834 --> 00:03:49,112
TAF can also be down.

56
00:03:49,162 --> 00:03:53,792
The platform checks its health at a set interval, and each call has a timeout.

57
00:03:53,842 --> 00:03:58,832
When TAF does not answer, the SMS vendor sends the code.

58
00:03:58,882 --> 00:04:00,968
The attempt is marked not scored.

59
00:04:01,018 --> 00:04:06,440
There is no verdict, no face confirmation, no ownership check, and no SIM match.

60
00:04:06,490 --> 00:04:12,560
The platform writes an audit event, tells the bank's antifraud system, and alerts operations.

61
00:04:12,610 --> 00:04:17,096
When TAF is back, the next code goes through TAF again.

62
00:04:17,146 --> 00:04:19,256
And one case is not an outage.

63
00:04:19,306 --> 00:04:23,624
On the state services portal, a person can choose one trusted bank.

64
00:04:23,674 --> 00:04:28,424
If a person chose a different bank, TAF refuses to send the code.

65
00:04:28,474 --> 00:04:33,368
The app tells the person to change the setting on the portal, or to contact the bank.

66
00:04:33,418 --> 00:04:36,320
Last, what TAF receives.

67
00:04:36,370 --> 00:04:42,536
The phone number, a request identifier, the code, the type of message, the device model and the language.

68
00:04:42,586 --> 00:04:46,760
The personal identification number goes only with the face confirmation.

69
00:04:46,810 --> 00:04:50,888
The phone ownership check sends only the identifier of the TAF part.

70
00:04:50,938 --> 00:04:54,920
Never a name, a document, an address or a photo.

71
00:04:54,970 --> 00:05:00,608
Now suppose TAF refuses a code because the person chose another bank on the portal.

72
00:05:00,658 --> 00:05:06,016
Does the SMS vendor send the code instead?

73
00:05:06,066 --> 00:05:12,496
No: the refusal is not an outage, so the platform stops and sends no code through any channel.

74
00:05:12,546 --> 00:05:16,840
In the master app, TAF sends the code and gives a verdict.

75
00:05:16,890 --> 00:05:21,928
The platform decides: Green continues, Yellow and Red refuse.

76
00:05:21,978 --> 00:05:26,176
When TAF is down, the code still comes, but not scored.

77
00:05:26,226 --> 00:05:29,464
When the person chose another bank, no code comes.

78
00:05:29,514 --> 00:05:33,376
Every one of these logins began with a password, before any code.

79
00:05:33,426 --> 00:05:37,096
Lesson 11 shows how the platform keeps that password.
